  "response": "## The finding\n\n`crime_00060` — `duplicate_component_shape`, medium / confidence 0.70, agent_risk 0.28, effort small.\n\n> \"div subtree appears in 4 files with the same structural shape.\"\n\nI read all four sites. The repeated subtree is the **form action bar** at the bottom of every invoice form:\n\n```tsx\n<div className=\"mt-6 flex justify-end gap-4\">\n  <Link\n    href=\"/dashboard/invoices\"\n    className=\"flex h-10 items-center rounded-lg bg-gray-100 px-4 text-sm font-medium text-gray-600 transition-colors hover:bg-gray-200\"\n  >\n    Cancel\n  </Link>\n  <Button type=\"submit\">Create Invoice</Button>\n</div>\n```\n\nA repo-wide grep confirms exactly four occurrences — no other call sites, so the extraction is closed-set.\n\n**The only thing that varies across all four copies is the submit label** (`Create Invoice` / `Edit Invoice`). The `href`, both className strings, the element order, and the `Cancel` text are byte-identical everywhere.\n\nThe drift the scenario describes is already visible, one block above the flagged subtree: `final-example/app/ui/invoices/create-form.tsx:138` uses `mt-2 text-sm text-red-500` for the form-level error, while `edit-form.tsx:148` uses `my-2 text-sm text-red-500`. Same block, hand-copied, one margin edited and not propagated.\n\n## Files that would change\n\n| File | Region |\n|---|---|\n| `dashboard/final-example/app/ui/invoices/create-form.tsx` | 142–150 |\n| `dashboard/final-example/app/ui/invoices/edit-form.tsx` | 152–160 |\n| `dashboard/starter-example/app/ui/invoices/create-form.tsx` | 101–109 |\n| `dashboard/starter-example/app/ui/invoices/edit-form.tsx` | 112–120 |\n\nPlus one new file **per app** — see the caveat below:\n\n- `dashboard/final-example/app/ui/invoices/form-actions.tsx` (new)\n- `dashboard/starter-example/app/ui/invoices/form-actions.tsx` (new)\n\n## Caveat: this is two consolidations, not one\n\n`final-example` and `starter-example` are **separate packages** — separate `package.json`, `tsconfig.json`, and `@/app/*` alias roots. The scan's `coverage.by_package` lists them as distinct. No shared component can span both without introducing a workspace package, which is out of proportion to a 9-line subtree.\n\nThey are also *deliberately* divergent: `starter-example/create-form.tsx` has no `'use client'`, no `useActionState`, no validation — it is the tutorial's \"before\" state that a learner edits. Consolidating inside the starter arguably works against what that copy is for.\n\n**Recommendation:** extract in `final-example` (2 call sites, real maintenance surface). Treat the starter copies as intentional variants and leave them, or mirror the same file if you want the two apps to stay structurally parallel. This is the \"confirm intentional variants first\" caution the detector's own `suggested_actions` carries.\n\n## Proposed shared component\n\n```tsx\n// app/ui/invoices/form-actions.tsx\nimport Link from 'next/link';\nimport { Button } from '@/app/ui/button';\n\nexport function FormActions({\n  submitLabel,\n  cancelHref = '/dashboard/invoices',\n  cancelLabel = 'Cancel',\n  children,\n}: {\n  submitLabel: string;\n  cancelHref?: string;\n  cancelLabel?: string;\n  children?: React.ReactNode;\n}) {\n  return (\n    <div className=\"mt-6 flex justify-end gap-4\">\n      {children}\n      <Link\n        href={cancelHref}\n        className=\"flex h-10 items-center rounded-lg bg-gray-100 px-4 text-sm font-medium text-gray-600 transition-colors hover:bg-gray-200\"\n      >\n        {cancelLabel}\n      </Link>\n      <Button type=\"submit\">{submitLabel}</Button>\n    </div>\n  );\n}\n```\n\n### Public API\n\n**Props**\n\n| Prop | Type | Required | Notes |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `submitLabel` | `string` | yes | The only value that actually differs today. Required, no default — a silent default would let a form ship the wrong verb. |\n| `cancelHref` | `string` | no, `'/dashboard/invoices'` | Identical in all four copies; defaulted rather than required so call sites stay one line. |\n| `cancelLabel` | `string` | no, `'Cancel'` | Included only as an i18n seam. |\n\n**Slots**\n\n| Slot | Type | Notes |\n|---|---|---|\n| `children` | `ReactNode` | Leading-actions slot, rendered left of Cancel inside the flex row. The obvious future occupant is a destructive action on the edit form (`DeleteInvoice` already exists in `app/ui/invoices/buttons.tsx`), which today lives in the table rather than the form. |\n\n### Call sites after the change\n\n```tsx\n<FormActions submitLabel=\"Create Invoice\" />\n<FormActions submitLabel=\"Edit Invoice\" />\n```\n\n### What I deliberately left out\n\n- **No `submit` slot / no pending state.** Nothing in these forms uses `useFormStatus` yet. When one does, replace `submitLabel: string` with `submitLabel: ReactNode` — additive, no call-site churn.\n- **No `className` override on the wrapper.** Four identical copies means there is no evidence of a second layout; an escape hatch here just recreates the drift.\n- **Not generalized beyond invoices.** `login-form.tsx` has a superficially similar footer but no Cancel link and different spacing. Pulling it in would be inventing a requirement.\n\nKeeping the file at `app/ui/invoices/` rather than `app/ui/` reflects that: it is the invoice form footer, and promoting it to app-wide is a decision for when a second domain needs it.\n\n## Adjacent, not part of this finding\n\nThe `<div id=\"{field}-error\" aria-live=\"polite\" aria-atomic=\"true\">` block repeats three times per file across both `final-example` forms (6 occurrences), and it is where the `mt-2`/`my-2` drift actually landed. A `<FieldError id errors />` component would be the higher-value extraction of the two. The detector didn't flag it — the three copies sit in one file each, below whatever cross-file threshold `duplicate_component_shape` uses. Flagging it here as a separate piece of work rather than folding it into `FormActions`, which would give the component two unrelated 